MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels especially right because Old Sock left me interested in relaxed, guitar-centered music, and this tribute continues that appeal.",
    "Terraplane feels like a natural next choice because its rootsy blues sound fits what I want now; In My Soul also connects with the soulful side of Memphis and Old Sock."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shadows in the Night and Beach Boys' Party! miss my current interest in guitar-driven blues: standards and an informal pop singalong offer different listening experiences.",
    "Loud Hailer's harder edge does not fit the relaxed mood I want today, while Muddy Wolf at Red Rocks interests me musically but loses out because I want a studio album this time."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Familiar melodic rock alone is not enough to make me choose New when my interest right now is more specifically blues.",
    "A blues guitar connection does not make every album equally appealing to me; intensity and the kind of performance matter too."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The relaxed feel that draws me from Old Sock toward The Breeze matters more today than guitar playing by itself.",
    "I can find several albums relevant and still choose only one or two; saving In My Soul or Old Yellow Moon for later does not mean their musical direction is wrong for me."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my blues and roots interests, but some missed my current preference for relaxed, guitar-centered studio listening."
}
